<title>FRANCE: Airbus says Thai Airways orders nine planes.</title>
<headline>Airbus says Thai Airways orders nine planes.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Airbus consortium said on Thursday that Thai Airways International had signed a contract for the firm order of four A330-300 and five A300-600R twin-engine widebody planes.</p>
<p>&quot;The A300-600Rs are scheduled for delivery from the first quarter of 1998, with A330 deliveries beginning in the second quarter of the year,&quot; Airbus said in a statement.</p>
</text>
